            ("Credentials are not instructions", "Authentication establishes who is calling; authorisation determines what that identity may do. Keep service secrets in an approved server-side environment and grant the narrowest practical access. Never put API keys in browser code, screenshots, prompts or a public repository."),
            ("Connectors and MCP", "A connector adapts a service to a workflow. MCP standardises certain interactions with tools and context; it is not itself a model, a privacy guarantee or a substitute for service permissions. A personal Claude subscription can cover eligible development usage while a deployed application's API calls require a separate approved arrangement."),
