            ("Efficiency techniques", "Quantisation uses lower-precision representations and can reduce memory at a possible quality trade-off. Distillation trains a smaller system using signals from another. Parameter-efficient adaptation updates selected components rather than all weights. Mixture-of-experts architectures route work among components. None of these terms alone establishes task quality or privacy."),
